# Repo-internal files — kept in the repo but not served on the public site.
#
# Cloudflare Pages deploys every committed file, which was publishing the
# migration guide (naming the Cloudflare account, Supabase project ref and
# deploy-token filename), the PowerShell scripts, and the raw brand kit.
# None of it is needed by the site; MIGRATION.md still has to live in the
# repo so the next machine move works from a clean clone.
#
# Format: <path> <destination> <status>.
# Pages supports only 301/302/303/307/308 here - 404 is silently ignored, so
# these send visitors to the homepage instead of exposing the file.
# Per Cloudflare's docs redirects are followed even when a static asset
# matches the request, so these do override the deployed files.

/MIGRATION.md                   /   301
/README.md                      /   301
/serve.ps1                      /   301
/deploy.ps1                     /   301
/deploy-github.ps1              /   301
/deploy-netlify-redirect.ps1    /   301

# Source brand kit: unreferenced by the site (fonts load from assets/fonts/),
# and contains licensed font files plus __MACOSX junk.
/brand-assets/*                 /   301

# Engine test harness — developer tooling, run locally via serve.ps1.
/tests/*                        /   301

# The /README.md rule above only covers the root one. This note explains how
# the sector photographs are sized and named — repo housekeeping, not a page.
/assets/sectors/README.md       /   301
